UAE PDPL Readiness for a Fintech Platform
Objectives
By completing this lab, you will:

Map personal data flows in a sample fintech system, including Emirates ID data
Document lawful bases for processing and a DPO appointment plan aligned to Federal Decree-Law 45 of 2021
Build simple consent and data subject rights (DSAR) handling scripts
Draft a breach notification procedure with timelines
Compile a UAE PDPL compliance dossier
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command-line familiarity
Basic Python 3 knowledge (functions, dictionaries, file I/O)
Conceptual understanding of data protection principles (lawful basis, consent, DSARs, breach notification)
No prior UAE PDPL expertise required, but review Federal Decree-Law 45 of 2021 summary before starting
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Linux machine via Start Lab. Run the following to prepare your workspace:

mkdir -p ~/pdpl-lab/{data,scripts,docs}
cd ~/pdpl-lab
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install pandas faker jsonschema
Verify Python and pip are working:

python3 --version
pip list | grep -E "pandas|faker|jsonschema"
